{"causes": ["The burgeoning Patrician cult in 7th-century Ireland spurred the collection and formalization of traditions related to Saint Patrick.", "The aspiration of the see of Armagh to assert its ecclesiastical primacy across Ireland necessitated historical and hagiographical justification.", "The existence of various oral traditions and perhaps earlier written fragments concerning Saint Patrick provided material for Tírechán's compilation."], "effects": ["Tírechán's *Collectanea* provided crucial textual support for the ecclesiastical claims of Armagh as the preeminent see in Ireland.", "His work became a foundational source for the hagiographical tradition of Saint Patrick, influencing subsequent accounts and popular understanding.", "The detailed accounts of Patrick's journeys and church foundations in the *Collectanea* contributed significantly to the mapping of early Christian sites in Ireland."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "tírechán", "sourceName": "Tírechán", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "early-irish-christian-traditions", "targetName": "Early Irish Christian Traditions", "context": "Tírechán compiled existing oral and written accounts of Saint Patrick in his *Collectanea* around 680-690 AD."}, {"sourceSlug": "tírechán", "sourceName": "Tírechán", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "collectanea-tirechan", "targetName": "Collectanea (Tírechán)", "context": "Tírechán authored the *Collectanea*, a significant Latin text detailing the life and mission of Saint Patrick, circa 680-690 AD."}, {"sourceSlug": "armagh-primacy", "sourceName": "Armagh Primacy", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "tírechán", "targetName": "Tírechán", "context": "Tírechán's *Collectanea* was written in part to support the claims of Armagh to ecclesiastical supremacy in Ireland during the late 7th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "tírechán", "sourceName": "Tírechán", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ireland", "targetName": "Ireland", "context": "Tírechán lived and worked as a bishop in 7th-century Ireland, primarily in the region of Connacht, where he documented Patrician sites."}, {"sourceSlug": "collectanea-tirechan", "sourceName": "Collectanea (Tírechán)", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "rise-of-armagh-primacy", "targetName": "Rise of Armagh Primacy", "context": "The *Collectanea* provided crucial historical and theological justification for Armagh's claims to be the metropolitan see of Ireland, strengthening its position."}], "places": [{"name": "Killala Bay, Ireland", "role": "Region of Origin"}, {"name": "Armagh, Ireland", "role": "Ecclesiastical Center Supported"}, {"name": "Ireland", "role": "Primary Sphere of Activity"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Tírechán", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "tírechán"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4001296", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%ADrech%C3%A1n"], "tags": ["Ireland", "Religious Figures", "Europe", "comparative-religion", "doctrine-development", "cultural-diffusion"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Tírechán's *Collectanea* provided one of the earliest and most influential written accounts of Saint Patrick, directly shaping the foundational narrative of Irish Christianity. His work was instrumental in establishing the ecclesiastical primacy of Armagh, a claim that profoundly influenced Irish church structure for centuries.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-05T07:00:48Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33949645931", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Tírechán was a 7th-century Irish bishop from north Connacht, specifically the Killala Bay area, in what is now County Mayo.", "newValue": "Tírechán, a 7th-century Irish bishop from north Connacht, specifically the Killala Bay area now in County Mayo, is primarily remembered as the author of the *Collectanea*, a crucial Latin text detailing the life and mission of Saint Patrick. Composed around 680-690 AD, Tírechán's work, along with Muirchú's *Vita S. Patricii*, represents the earliest substantial written accounts of Ireland's patron saint. His writings are invaluable for understanding the development of early Irish Christianity and the Patrician cult, particularly in their efforts to establish the ecclesiastical primacy of Armagh.

The *Collectanea* is not a single, cohesive narrative but a compilation of diverse traditions, miracles, and land grants attributed to Patrick. It vividly recounts Patrick's journeys across Ireland, his baptisms of kings and commoners, the foundations of numerous churches, and his confrontations with pagan druids and local chieftains. Tírechán meticulously lists places associated with Patrick's activities and details the saint's spiritual authority, often presenting miraculous interventions. This collection, preserved in the 9th-century Book of Armagh, provides a unique window into the geographical and social landscape of 7th-century Ireland, albeit through a hagiographical lens.

The lasting legacy of Tírechán's *Collectanea* lies in its profound influence on the perception of Saint Patrick and the institutional development of the Irish Church. It helped solidify the narrative of Patrick as the singular apostle of Ireland and provided foundational justification for the claims of Armagh to be the metropolitan see, inheriting Patrick's authority. This text, by shaping the Patrician legend and validating Armagh's preeminence, profoundly impacted subsequent Irish hagiography, ecclesiastical politics, and national identity for centuries, becoming a cornerstone of early medieval Irish historical understanding."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-05T07:00:48Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33949645931", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "Classical"}, {"title": "Spiritual seeking and religious community formation", "type": "Idea", "year": ""}], "newValue": ["The burgeoning Patrician cult in 7th-century Ireland spurred the collection and formalization of traditions related to Saint Patrick.", "The aspiration of the see of Armagh to assert its ecclesiastical primacy across Ireland necessitated historical and hagiographical justification.", "The existence of various oral traditions and perhaps earlier written fragments concerning Saint Patrick provided material for Tírechán's compilation."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-05T07:00:48Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33949645931", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped religious practice and spiritual communities", "type": "Idea", "year": ""}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "Classical"}], "newValue": ["Tírechán's *Collectanea* provided crucial textual support for the ecclesiastical claims of Armagh as the preeminent see in Ire